course: dictionary
lesson: 8228
title: Words that go back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To revert means to go back to how something was before. «People revert to old habits when they are tired» means they slip back into habits they had given up. Revert is a verb, so it can change: revert, reverts, reverted, reverting.
explain: On a computer, to revert means to undo changes and return to an earlier version. When someone adds wrong facts to a page, an editor may revert the page. Check the meaning by swapping in "undo the changes and go back to the earlier version": if it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Be careful with revert in Indian English. The example says «"revert" often means reply», so "I will revert to you" means "I will reply to you". Many speakers elsewhere think this use is wrong, so look at the words around it before you decide what it means.
fact: Revert means to go back to an earlier state, habit or way of doing things.
fact: On a computer, to revert means to undo changes and return to an earlier version of a file or page.
fact: In law, property can revert, which means it goes back to its first owner.
fact: In Indian English, revert often means reply, but many speakers elsewhere think this use is wrong.
fact: "Revert back" is common, but it repeats the idea, because revert already means "back".
exercise: «People revert to old habits when they are tired.» What does revert mean here? | Forget every habit they have | Make a brand new habit | Start a race | *Go back to an old habit
exercise: An editor sees wrong facts added to a Wikipedia page. What might they do? | *Revert the changes to an earlier version | Delete the whole internet | Add even more wrong facts | Print the page in colour
exercise: A friend in India writes, «I will revert to you tomorrow.» What does revert probably mean? | Forget about you | *Reply | Go back in time | Own the land again
test: «The garden slowly reverted to wild, with weeds where the roses had been.» What does reverted mean? | Became a neat, tidy park | Was painted bright green | *Went back to a wild state | Turned into a lake
test: When a gift of land ends, the land reverts to its first owner. What does reverts mean? | Is given to the school | Is painted green | Is sold to a stranger | *Goes back to the first owner
exam: In Indian English, «Please revert by Friday» means what? | Please go back in time by Friday | Please forget all about it by Friday | Please undo everything by Friday | *Please reply by Friday
